# Symbol-level govulncheck findings accepted for this fork.
# Format: one OSV ID per line. Everything not listed here fails CI.
#
# All four are vulnerabilities in the Prometheus *server* (web UI stored XSS,
# remote-read snappy DoS, Azure AD remote-write secret exposure via the config
# API). They are pulled in transitively through madmin-go and are only reported
# as reachable via package init (controller.init -> madmin.init ->
# histogram.init). The operator runs no Prometheus server, web UI, remote-read
# endpoint or Azure AD remote write, so none of them is exploitable here.
# Fixing them needs github.com/prometheus/prometheus >= v0.311.3, which drags
# k8s.io/* from v0.32 to v0.35 - too invasive for a fork that only carries the
# leader-election shutdown fix. Drop these once upstream bumps Prometheus.
